test-stream-inheritance.js: language non-goal (§13); every assertion observes or mutates constructor/prototype-chain identity through `instanceof`, `.prototype`, or `Object.setPrototypeOf`, including Node's prototype-copying emulation of multiple inheritance
test-stream-iter-cross-realm.js: language non-goal (§13); every case constructs the value under test in a separate `vm` context and specifically measures cross-realm identity/recognition
test-stream-iter-disabled.js: host-binary subprocess; every assertion launches a fresh Node process and measures that binary's `--experimental-stream-iter` module-registration flag, so the substituted stream module is never loaded
test-stream-iter-readable-interop-disabled.js: host-binary subprocess; every assertion launches a fresh Node process and measures that binary's `--experimental-stream-iter` flag or builtin module registry, so the substituted stream module is never loaded
test-stream2-readable-wrap-proxy-methods.js: language non-goal (§13); the entire regression dynamically enumerates arbitrary own method names, installs forwarding properties on another object, and compares prototype-owned function identity, which requires the runtime property map/prototype metaobject model
test-stream-consumers.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); four object-mode Blob/arrayBuffer/buffer/bytes cases require Web-IDL to invoke arbitrary object ToPrimitive/prototype conversion and their unhandled rejection aborts the file before its ordinary promise assertions settle; local/consumers-static.js retains classic and Web byte/string/JSON consumption, malformed and incomplete UTF-8, stream locking, and typed object-mode rejection
test-stream-iter-broadcast-basic.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); the final overlapping-next regression deep-compares four null-prototype record literals, while local/broadcast-basic-static.js retains all seventeen broadcast state, backpressure, abort, failure, cancellation, late-consumer, and overlapping-read cases without observing prototypes
test-stream-iter-readable-interop.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); it directly inspects Readable.prototype and distinguishes Buffer from Uint8Array solely by prototype identity; local/iter-readable-interop-static.js retains every other classic byte/object adaptation, batching, protocol, transform, collection, cancellation, identity, error, and zlib/iter integration assertion against this implementation
test-stream-pipe-same-destination-twice.js: mixed language non-goal (§13); every phase indexes `_events.data` as Node's dynamic internal property bag, which this implementation deliberately represents as a typed Map; local/pipe-same-destination-static.js retains duplicate pipe entries, one-at-a-time unpipe, exact delivery counts, and complete removal
test-stream-pipeline.js: mixed language non-goal (§13) and host-module integration; it extracts and invokes a host fs method through Function.call and later requires single-access getter-backed arbitrary-thenable dispatch through Function.prototype; local/pipeline-static.js plus the dedicated untouched pipeline fixtures retain stream/function stages, result propagation, teardown, abort, array form, and end:false behavior
test-stream-readable-async-iterators.js: mixed language non-goal (§13) and host-module integration; it dynamically grafts Readable.prototype[Symbol.asyncIterator] onto v1 streams, invokes that prototype method and extracted destroy functions through Function.call, mutates public method slots, observes Node's dynamically attached iterator.stream property, and later iterates host fs/http streams; local/readable-async-iterators-static.js retains every ordinary Readable iteration, concurrent-next, error, premature-close, end, transform, autoDestroy, and destroyOnReturn assertion without those engine/host dependencies
test-stream-preprocess.js: upstream ownership mismatch; the file never imports stream and tests BOM preprocessing exclusively through readline.createInterface over host fs streams, so its stream-lane pass is hollow; it is exercised against this repository's readline implementation through runtime/node/readline/extra-tests
test-stream2-httpclient-response-end.js: upstream ownership mismatch; the file never imports stream and tests readable/end delivery exclusively on an HTTP client response produced by http.createServer/http.get, so its stream-lane pass is hollow; it is exercised against this repository's HTTP implementation through runtime/node/http/extra-tests
test-global-webstreams.js: hollow by construction; both sides are Node's own -- `shape.mjs:91` assigns the platform `node:stream/web` namespace and the globals it is compared against are the same objects, so the file cannot report anything about this artifact until Web Streams are implemented here rather than bridged
test-stream-aliases-legacy.js: hollow oracle; `stream.Readable` and `require('_stream_readable')` are both `undefined` in the ordinary run, so the five identity assertions compare absences and pass; local/legacy-alias-identity-static.js requires each alias to construct an instance of its class before retaining them, and fails until they exist
